<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>AI Writing Assistance Statement</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Large language models were utilized solely for minor linguistic improvements, including enhanced phrasing and clarity. These tools played no role in content generation, experimental design, data analysis, or interpretation. The authors are entirely responsible for all ideas, results, and conclusions presented in this paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>More Details on CHAIR</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we report <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CHAIR}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CHAIR}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CHAIR}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CHAIR}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> as evaluation metrics. The calculation of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CHAIR}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CHAIR}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{CHAIR}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{CHAIR}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> is shown in Equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="In A.2 More Details on CHAIR ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Dynamic Multimodal Activation Steering for Hallucination Mitigation in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, where we set the maximum number of new tokens to 512 in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{CHAIR}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{CHAIR}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{|\{\text{sentences with hallucinated objects}\}|}{|\{\text{all sentences}\}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>sentences with hallucinated objects</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>all sentences</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{|\{\text{sentences with hallucinated objects}\}|}{|\{\text{all sentences}\}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{CHAIR}_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>CHAIR</mtext><mi>I</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{CHAIR}_{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{|\{\text{hallucinated objects}\}|}{|\{\text{all objects mentioned}\}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>hallucinated objects</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>all objects mentioned</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{|\{\text{hallucinated objects}\}|}{|\{\text{all objects mentioned}\}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Results on POPE</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complete experimental results on POPE are presented in Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.3 Results on POPE ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Dynamic Multimodal Activation Steering for Hallucination Mitigation in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Our method achieves significant improvements across all three experimental settings: random, popular, and adversarial.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A1.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A1.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
