<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Results on AMBER</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an evaluation of LLaVA v1.5 on the AMBER <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. AMBER contains both discriminative tasks and generative tasks. The experimental results are shown in Table <a href="#A1.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ A.4 Results on AMBER ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Dynamic Multimodal Activation Steering for Hallucination Mitigation in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. Our method outperforms existing methods on both discriminative and generative tasks, achieving significant effects in hallucination mitigation.</p>
</div>
