<section id="A1.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.10 </span>Experiments on different decoding strategies</h3>

<div id="A1.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To explore the effectiveness of our method under different decoding strategies, including beam search (beam=2), nucleus sampling (temperature=0.5, topp=0.7) and greedy search, the results on MME and MMVP benchmarks are presented in the Table <a href="#A1.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ A.10 Experiments on different decoding strategies ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Dynamic Multimodal Activation Steering for Hallucination Mitigation in Large Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. Our method consistently demonstrates effective hallucination mitigation across all decoding settings, confirming the robustness of our approach.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T12" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A1.T12.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:435.1pt;height:88.9pt;vertical-align:-42.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-24.2pt,4.9pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<table id="A1.T12.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A1.T12.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
